    "body": "Back to draft: #412 (#321) added its own `CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL`, which refuses a lathe or mill-turn part flip and is pinned in `carried_fixtures_cache`. That is the **same name** as this PR's different-machines refusal, so the two collide in `stock_sim_carry.rs`. Resolved:\n- #412's constant keeps its name and meaning.\n- This PR's constant is renamed **`CARRY_MACHINE_CHANGE_REFUSAL`** in the code, the re-export, `setup_carry` and the 404 decision file.\n- `carry_turn()` now runs #404's `one_machine` check first, then the kind check on the two setups' shared machine with #412's message.\n\nPassing: `setup_carry` 8, `carried_fixtures_cache` 6, `rest_across_setups` 7, `stock_sim_document` 9, `carried_verify` 8, `setups` 11. The only red is `setup_stock_source`'s new-block test, which is #415 on main (fixed by #420). Re-gating, then flagging ready again.",
